        <section>
            <h2>About TextDrop</h2>
            <p>TextDrop is a small tool for getting text and structure out of PDF files. Whether you need the text of a page, the words inside one box on it, or the tables it contains, TextDrop shows you what the PDF holds and lets you copy it out.</p>
            <p>It is also an example application for the <a href="https://github.com/francis-build/francis">Francis</a> web framework, built on the <a href="https://hex.pm/packages/pdf_extractor">pdf_extractor</a> library.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h2>How to Use TextDrop</h2>
            <ol>
                <li>Upload your PDF file using the <a href="/#upload_form">upload form</a>. You land on the document page with its metadata and the size of every page.</li>
                <li>Pick a page. Its text appears next to the preview; tick <em>Keep layout</em> to preserve the columns.</li>
                <li>Drag on the preview to draw areas, then extract the text inside each one.</li>
                <li>Load the words to see every word's box, font and size, or find the tables on the page and read them as rows.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>
